My second ascension, this game was much more fun then my first one as a
rogue as it was much more of a challenge. The quest artifact is much
better than the rogues, I was using it a lot for charging various wands
throughout the game. After the castle, the only bit of difficulty I had
was on the plane of air, where I was killed by a air elemental, using
up one of my amulets of life saving. On the Astral Plane, the Angel
generated started attacking me even though I wasn't wearing a ring of
conflict, and so I was forced to kill it. Any reason why this should
be? I was not causing conflict, and hadn't hit it with anything. Below
are the notes I took during the game, with a couple of modifications.

Dlvl 1 - kitten left there as I wanted to play petless, never saw it
again or tamed another monster in the whole game.

Dlvl 3 - a neutral altar, as I had plenty of food I decided to hang
about sacrificing and was given Magicbane after about 1000 turns, this
was my primary weapon for the rest of the game.

Dlvl 4 - a bones pile from an unlucky priest gave me a cursed +0 robe,
uncursed spellbooks of identify and light and 4 potions of holy water.
I took all this back to the altar, blessed and read the spellbooks and
uncursed and wore the robe. Hung around on level 3 casting light until
my divination skill went to basic, and I could cast identify with 0%
failure while wearing the robe. The mines entrance was on this level,
decided to go down to minetown in hope of a wish.

Minetown - nothing of interest, no magic lamp, BoH or magic whistle and
the altar was lawful. Came back up to the main dungeon, and never
finished the mines. On the way down to minetown I got dwarvish-mithril,
a dwarvish helm, iron shoes and 18 +0 daggers which went into my
quiver.

Sokoban - gave me the amulet of reflection and rings of polymorph
control and slow digestion.

Dlvl 14 - the entrance to the quest, found a helm of telepathy on this
level. Went to the castle before the quest to get my experience up.

Dlvl 16 - a bones pile gave me most of the ascension kit, including +3
SDSM, fixed +3 speed boots, a +2 helm of brilliance, a luckstone and a
blessed bag of holding which sloved the inventory problems I'd been
having. I also found a amulet of life saving, which I exchanged for the
amulet of reflection I had been wearing.

The Castle - the wand gave me 2 scrolls of charging, 2 scrolls of
genocide which were used on L's and h's, a blessed +3 silver dagger to
twoweapon with Magicbane, a magic marker to enchant my armour with, a
spellbook of magic mapping to use in gehennom, the Eye of the
Aethiopica to help with spellcasting and the last wish was eventually
used in the VotD on a tin of red dragon meat to get fire resistance. I
also found a ring of polymorph, so I went into a corner, stripped off
and laid a load of cockatice eggs which came in very useful over the
game.

Back to the quest - the quest nemesis was easy, I just kept chucking +5
daggers at him until he died. I was suprised at all the shops,
unfortunatley they had nothing good for sale.

Gehennom went by fairly easily, I got the magic mapping failure rate to
about 62% with the robe on, and the eye of the aethiopica meant I could
keep trying much faster. I kept recharging my wands of digging with the
PYEC to clear routes between the stairs. The major demons mostly went
down to thrown cockatrice eggs, as did the Wizard. The high priest I
think was killed by my wand of death. On the way back up, the
mysterious force wasn't so bad as my rogue, although it was annoying.

My altar on the astral plane was the middle one, which was guarded by
Famine.  I kept hitting him until he went down, the unfriendly priests
all got turned to stone with my flying cockatrice eggs.


